# The add-on ships a committed build context, so `npm run build:addon` has to
# produce the same bytes on every machine. Vite copies `index.html` through from
# source while injecting its own script tags with LF, so a CRLF checkout yields
# output that no amount of post-processing can reconcile with a LF one. Check
# every text file out with LF so the build is reproducible across platforms.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts run inside the add-on's Alpine container. A CRLF line ending
# turns the shebang into `#!/bin/sh\r`, which the kernel resolves to a program
# name that does not exist — the container then dies with a bare
# "no such file or directory". Force LF on checkout, on every platform.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The staged add-on build context is generated output that is committed so
# Supervisor can clone and build this repository as-is. Treat it as opaque: with
# line-ending conversion on, a Windows checkout would rewrite these files and
# `npm run check:addon` would report a difference that is not really there.
addon/rootfs/app/** -text
